{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-quasi-finite-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-locally-quasi-compact}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7441f8c3881d99b2d112e50c8c45cdfd255d2d3cc722e77a059c02362231a99", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e7ea4136f942d0418bf17ec56df27992de312b68782118382e054f53673dbaff", "source_text": "The first and second assertion follow from the corresponding\nalgebra result, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\n(combined with the fact that <MATH_0001> is also locally of finite type by\nLemma <REF_0002>).\nBy the above, Lemma <REF_0003>\nand the fact that a base change of a\nquasi-compact morphism is quasi-compact, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0004>\nwe see that the base change of a quasi-finite morphism\nis quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c8b2de50b349c6a305028b203930844aec34dddca5f851893a0786ba750ccb6", "unit_id": "tag:01TM:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$s$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite-at-a-finite-number-of-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:841aa9ca852def4d5cd19b05e096b52ecdc87ddb95fc2dca44f64c3348079c7b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ac1b7879e154066ec1e69341ac7a01ee48d48e7a5bae8f21d4651be8b3f5f9d9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes of finite type.\nLet <MATH_0002>. There are at most finitely many points\nof <MATH_0003> lying over <MATH_0004> at which <MATH_0005> is quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:20b687add44bccdb0dc79cc7083c37b7035cef1e5570ffbf661781979fd54be0", "unit_id": "tag:0AAY:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X_s$", "MATH_0002": "$X_s$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-noetherian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8f0dccf0ac28368d65f92a22801677323f98b8d248b9eef56ab67db9c6416e4f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ca44ae254a90842d07c72b10b5c82b967ae19ebd3557838909459a621f9f3bc", "source_text": "The fibre <MATH_0001> is a scheme of finite type over a field,\nhence Noetherian (Lemma <REF_0001>).\nHence the topology on <MATH_0002> is Noetherian (Properties, Lemma\n<REF_0002>)\nand can have at most a finite number of isolated points (by elementary\ntopology). Thus our lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:775ec16c958fb6b4ef58de131036c1f5f0881c8435e2f5f0f04bd87e5b7e7249", "unit_id": "tag:0AAY:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-monomorphism-loc-finite-type-loc-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a07bb346fb3b8a2c9985282f7fa56619acfc9423bc66525cd6b2506ac6d7c18f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1d12885f22b5983db519075050cdf40513ceab606fa95e584fbcb6d874b43b9b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0002> is locally of finite type and a monomorphism, then <MATH_0003>\nis separated and locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:62d5c944396c16f9467d0b25c0b3da31fe36b2b66fc023d0f99171e8c39e77f6", "unit_id": "tag:0CT8:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-monomorphism-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de06a4290a752f5c38aa0af4f3034b75324e73db32efab6e94b2544a8a275235", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab3b32450fae51ae7b2afb4852e179b14f5f1d840031be6a95f94aa0584ab92c", "source_text": "A monomorphism is separated by Schemes, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nA monomorphism is injective, hence we get <MATH_0001>\nis quasi-finite at every <MATH_0002> for example by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:31176d6f0ebde185a19f5a7a832047aa44c01e7b424222e6508d7b1924fafe85", "unit_id": "tag:0CT8:proof"}
